{"kind":"request","text":"codex: put the cause of staleness on the row, so an actor can see why a record is stale without walking provenance by hand. Hugh reassigned this to you today; it was parked on ox-builder, who has been silent all session. I am retiring the stale original 841d812a beside this filing.\n\nWHY IT IS BEING REFILED RATHER THAN RESUMED. The original went stale and its whole artifact chain with it. Two heads were reviewed under it — ed3c25e6 approved, then c9280b32 which took an approval and then a changes-requested — and neither is in main. I checked rather than assumed: git merge-base says both are outside main, and grep for stale_because and StaleBecause across internal/statusview, internal/workroom and ui/src in main returns nothing. So the work is genuinely unshipped, not shipped-and-forgotten. Treat those old heads as history, not as a base to rebase onto; the last verdict on that lane asked for changes and I would not want you inheriting an unread objection.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT, which is the part worth keeping from the original. Taken from the live projection rather than assumed: statement rows carry stale, and where it applies describes_superseded_world and world_superseded_at, but nothing saying which basis died. Walking the last 300 stale statements, every one had a retired basis within five hops, 164 at exactly one hop and 101 at two. The cause is nearly always adjacent, so computing it is a short bounded walk rather than a graph traversal anyone should fear. Re-measure before you build; the log has moved by roughly two thousand records since that count and I would rather you trust your own number.\n\nWHY I STILL WANT THIS. Twice today I reasoned wrongly from a row because the row did not carry what I needed. I read rests_on off a projection statement, got nothing, and nearly retired a request on the strength of it — the field is not on the row at all, it lives in a side table. That is worse than absent, because absence invites a confident wrong answer rather than a second question. This request is the read-side fix for exactly that class.\n\nTHE SECOND QUESTION IS STILL YOURS TO JUDGE, and I have not pre-decided it. The projection carries a top-level provenance map; the data is present but not on the row. Whether the fix is an inline bases field, a note in the surface documentation that provenance is a side table, or something else, is your call. I do not want every row inflated with its bases if that costs more than it returns, and you know the bounds work better than I do.\n\nNot urgent. Sequence it behind the identifier consolidation now under review at 500bc9b1 and behind anything the chess lanes need.","body":{"conditions":"Rows carrying stale also carry the nearest retired basis by event id, with its path when that basis is an artifact, bounded by a stated hop limit that reports its own exhaustion rather than a wrong nearest. Re-measure the hop distribution at the current log before building, and state the figure you measured rather than carrying forward the 164-at-one-hop count from the original request. Record a judgement, as an assert or in the head, on whether provenance should also be legible from the row itself or documented as a side table, with the reason. Mutation-sensitive tests covering the one-hop case, a multi-hop case, and the limit-exhausted case; prove sensitivity by breaking the walk at its decision site, watching the named assertion fail, and reverting. Exact clean pushed head, per-path artifacts at every changed stable path, gofmt, build, vet and go test ./... -count=1 green, and independent review recording Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Do not merge. Sequenced after the identifier consolidation at 500bc9b1 and after the chess lanes; nothing here is urgent.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}